-- title:
--   The (1,0)-branch prime is cut out by vanishing q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a positive integer $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{q\ell\}$, let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, let $\xi \in L$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and assume $\zeta = \xi^{\ell}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$), with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$ coming from $\ell \mid q^2M'$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((T))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A \to L \to K$, and let $\varpi$ be a generator of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$, $j \neq 0$, be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $T^{-1}\cdot(\text{numerator series})$ of the modular invariant. Write $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the scheme obtained as the pushout of the two chart inclusions, the finite chart being $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin A K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and the infinite chart the analogous one for $j^{-1}$.
--
--   Let $z$ be a point of $\mathfrak{X}$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism $\mathfrak{X} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ on global sections; it is assumed that $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$. Let $y$ be a point of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ with $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(y) = z$. The hypothesis `hss` requires that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A K j` to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-trivial point killed by $q$.
--
--   Let $W$ be a discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, and let $\sigma : A \to W$ be a ring homomorphism with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$. Let $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1 \pmod{(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}}$, the congruence being modulo the $(q+2)$-nd power of the ideal generated by $X_0, X_1$; here $X_0X_1^{\,q} - X_0^{\,q}X_1$ is [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18). Finally let
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma\varpi)\,v - f\,u\bigr)$$
--   be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of the stalk at its maximal ideal onto $S$.
--
--   Throughout, `STK` denotes the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{\mathfrak{X},z}$, `CMP` its adic completion, `toC` the canonical map $\mathrm{STK} \to \mathrm{CMP}$, `mkS` the quotient map $W[[X_0,X_1]] \to S$, and `germY` the ring homomorphism from `chartAlgFin A K j` to the stalk obtained by composing the inverse of the global-sections isomorphism of $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin A K j`, the inverse of the comparison isomorphism of $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}$ on $\top$, and the germ map at $z$ on the open set $\iota_{\mathrm{fin}}(\top)$.
--
--   Five groups of hypotheses on these data are imposed. The constants clause `hconst` requires that for every $a \in A$ the isomorphism $e$ carries the image in the completion of the germ at $z$ of $a$ (pulled back along $\mathfrak{X} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$) to the class of the constant series $C(\sigma a)$. The two stability clauses concern, for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, the $L$-algebra automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ with [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), that is: for every weight $k$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ admitting integral $q$-expansion series $p_f, p_g$ with $p_g$ having non-zero image, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of the two series, and every ring embedding $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota\zeta = e^{2\pi i/q}$, the series $\iota(\tau x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} \delta_{00} & \delta_{01}/q \\ q\,\delta_{10} & \delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$. The clause `hfin` requires every such $\tau$ to map `chartAlgFin A K j` into itself; the clause `hfix` requires, for those $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ and any proof of the preservation property, that the induced endomorphism of `chartAlgFin A K j` satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in \mathfrak{p}_y$ for all $a$.
--
--   The linearisation clause `hlin` requires: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ as above attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, every proof that $\tau$ preserves `chartAlgFin A K j`, and under the assumption that the resulting endomorphism satisfies $\tau(a) - a \in \mathfrak{p}_y$ for all $a$, there exist a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in \mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that (i) $\theta$ is compatible with $\tau$ through $e \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germY}$ on `chartAlgFin A K j`; (ii) $\theta$ fixes the class of every constant series $C(w)$, $w \in W$; (iii) for each index $jj$, $\theta(\mathrm{mkS}\,X_{jj}) - \mathrm{mkS}\bigl(\sum_{ii} C(M_{ii\,jj})X_{ii}\bigr)$ lies in the square of the ideal of $S$ generated by $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$; (iv) $c^{q+1} - 1 \in \mathfrak{m}_W$; (v) $M_{ii\,jj} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ii\,jj} \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$ for all $ii, jj$; (vi) if $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \pmod{\ell}$ then $c \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_W}$; and (vii) if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau$ is not the identity on $K$ then $c - 1 \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   The separation clause `hdist` requires: for all integers $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ and all primes $P_1, P_2$ of $S$ such that for each $P_i$ at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$ lies outside $P_i$, such that $\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma\varpi) \in P_i$, and such that $P_i$ contains the class of $C(a_i)X_0 + C(b_i)X_1 + h_i$ for some $h_i \in (X_0,X_1)^2$, if $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$ then the contractions of $P_1$ and $P_2$ along $\mathrm{toC}$ followed by $e$ are distinct ideals of the stalk.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $P$ be a prime ideal of $S$ such that at least one of $\mathrm{mkS}\,X_0, \mathrm{mkS}\,X_1$ lies outside $P$, such that $\mathrm{mkS}\,C(\sigma\varpi) \in P$, and such that there exists $h$ in the square of the ideal $(X_0, X_1) \subseteq W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with the class of $C(1)X_0 + C(0)X_1 + h$ lying in $P$ — the branch with tangent direction $(1,0)$. Then for every $a$ in `chartAlgFin A K j`,
--   $$e\bigl(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)\bigr) \in P \iff \text{for every } n \in \mathbb{Z} \text{ there is } m \in \mathfrak{m}_A \text{ with } \mathrm{coeff}_n\bigl(a\bigr) = \mathrm{algebraMap}\,A\,L\,(m),$$
--   where $\mathrm{coeff}_n(a)$ denotes the $n$-th coefficient of the Laurent series in $L$ attached to $a$; the membership on the left is stated as $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ belonging to the contraction of $P$ along $e$.
--
--   This is the branch-anchoring step for the Drinfeld local chart at a supersingular point of the integral two-chart model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-frame at a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, valid for all primes $q$ including $q = 2, 3$: of the two branches through the supersingular point, the one with tangent direction $(1,0)$ is exactly the Igusa-type branch along which all $q$-expansion coefficients of a function on the finite chart are divisible by the uniformiser of $A$. It is used by the theorem producing a completed-stalk chart carrying the full list of riders, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_of_levelAut_riders_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd).
